Feature: Masking last 4 digits of invoice_number in the d_product_revenue_clone table

  Background: Prepare the environment
    Given the table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone exists
    When I drop the table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone if it exists
    Then I create a replica of purgo_playground.d_product_revenue as purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone

  Scenario: Mask the last 4 digits of invoice_number for valid invoice numbers
    Given the table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone has data
    When the invoice_number column contains a 10-digit number
    Then mask the last 4 digits with asterisks
    And store the masked value back in the invoice_number column
    And all other columns remain unchanged

  Scenario: Skip masking for non-10-digit invoice numbers
    Given the table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone has data
    When the invoice_number column does not contain a 10-digit number
    Then do not apply any masking
    And retain the original invoice_number

  Scenario Outline: Handle null or empty invoice_number
    Given the table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone has data
    When the invoice_number is "<value>"
    Then set the invoice_number to null

    Examples:
      | value |
      | null  |
      | ""    |

  Scenario: Error handling during masking operation
    Given the table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone has data
    When a runtime error occurs during masking
    Then log the error message "Error processing invoice_number: <error_message>"

  Scenario Outline: Verify masking operation with example data
    Given the potential invoice_number "<original_value>"
    When masking logic is applied
    Then the masked invoice_number should be "<masked_value>"

    Examples:
      | original_value | masked_value |
      | 1234234534     | 123423****   |
      | 9876543210     | 987654****   |
      | 1111222233     | 111122****   |

